    },
    "/runs": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Accept a workflow and answer immediately with something to poll.\n\nThe uploads are read here, while the request is still open. By the time the\nwork runs there is no request left to read them from -- which is the whole\ndifference between this and /convert, and the reason it cannot simply call\nthe same handler in the background.",
        "operationId": "submit_run_runs_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "multipart/form-data": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Body_submit_run_runs_post"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "202": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Submit Run"
      }
    },
    "/runs/{run_id}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Where a run has got to, and its outputs once it is COMPLETE.",
        "operationId": "get_run_runs__run_id__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "run_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Run Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get Run"
      }
    },
    "/runs/{run_id}/cancel": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Ask a run to stop, and end the processes doing it.\n\nThe path is WES's, so exposing this as a WES endpoint later (F5) does not\nmove it.\n\nTwo shapes of run, and they differ. One waiting for a slot has executed\nnothing, so cancelling it is a matter of state: it settles CANCELED when its\nturn comes and it declines to start. One that is running has a process\ngroup, and that group is ended -- the tool and everything it spawned,\nexactly as the timeout does it, because a tool that spawns children and\nsurvives its parent is the reason group-killing is there at all.\n\nThe reply is CANCELING rather than CANCELED, and that is not evasion: the\nkill has been issued, but the run is not over until the worker has finished\ntidying up and said so. Reporting CANCELED here would be claiming something\nthat has not happened yet.",
        "operationId": "cancel_run_runs__run_id__cancel_post",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "run_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Run Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Cancel Run"
      }
    },
    "/runs/{run_id}/logs": {
      "get": {
        "description": "What the run printed, and which step snakemake blamed.\n\nTwo halves, and the response says which is which rather than blurring them.\n`steps` names the nodes that FAILED, because snakemake states that outright.\nA step that succeeded is not separated out: its output is in `stdout` along\nwith everything else's, and nothing marks where one rule's writing ends.\nSplitting that needs a log: directive per rule, which is the emitter's\nbusiness.\n\nAvailable while a run is still going, not only at the end -- there is no\nreason to make someone wait for a fifteen-minute run to finish before seeing\nwhat it has said so far.",
        "operationId": "get_run_logs_runs__run_id__logs_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "run_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Run Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get Run Logs"
      }
    },
    "/runs/{run_id}/manifest": {
      "get": {
        "description": "How this run was produced, in enough detail to attempt it again.\n\nThe workflow by digest, each tool by the digests the registry stated for it,\nevery input and output by content, the runner and image, and the exit code.\n\nWhat it does not claim is that re-execution is guaranteed. A tool that reads\nthe clock or the network will not reproduce, and the manifest records what\nwas fixed rather than promising that was everything.",
        "operationId": "get_run_manifest_runs__run_id__manifest_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "run_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Run Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Get Run Manifest"
      }
    },
    "/runs/{run_id}/outputs/{node_id}/{handle}": {
      "get": {
        "description": "One output, streamed, without base64 and without holding it in memory.\n\nThe endpoint D2 needs. /convert and /runs still return everything encoded in\none response, because that is the contract the editor speaks -- but an\noutput larger than memory cannot come back that way, and this is how it\ncomes back instead.\n\nA client names a node and a handle, never a path. What those mean is read\nfrom what the run recorded, so nothing a caller sends decides which file is\nopened, and the file is opened through the workspace -- so a tool that\nreplaced its own output with a symlink still cannot have the target's\ncontents served (#41).",
        "operationId": "stream_output_runs__run_id__outputs__node_id___handle__get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "run_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Run Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "node_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Node Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "handle",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Handle",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {}
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "summary": "Stream Output"
      }
    }
  }
}
